Applied to the R12 with hypothetical notes (a diatonic row in G, not yet confirmed), the window is reachable with machinable dimensions only for chambers 8 to 10. The low chambers, 1 to 7, have resonances 2.4 to 7.8 times their notes and would need an enormous chamber or a minute hole; for them the proposal only moves the resonance at least 50 cents away from the harmonics 1 to 6 of the notes, so that it pulls neither pitch nor timbre, and three chambers (3, 4 and 7) have their A-against-B mode within 20 cents of a harmonic. The two highest chambers carry a note above their resonance, which does not start in the model; chamber 12 would need a smaller volume than the bounds allow. All of this is a proposal written to a file, nothing has been changed in the drawing, and the notes are a hypothesis: as soon as the real notes are in notes_r12.csv everything recomputes itself.
